  "body": "Replaces #82 (closed automatically when its stacked base, #78, merged and the base branch was deleted). Same branch and commits; #78 is on main.\n\nP0 (#77): on a mill-turn the cross drill posted silently with its rapids 5 mm inside uncut raw stock.\n\n**Before** (r10 bar in r20 cylinder stock, holes at +X, +Y, -X): standoff measured from the part only - start and approach at r15, station-change rapid `G00 X21.213 Y0 Z10 -> G00 X0 Y21.213 Z0` passing r15 from the spindle. Mill-turn: the verification gate returned no warnings (the rapid-in-stock check is off for radial drilling - filed as #79) and the post went through. Lathe: blocked only by an unrelated false refusal (#80).\n\n**What changed**\n- New `crates/app/src/operation/cross_stock.rs`: measures the part and the setup's stock about the same spindle line `cross_spindle.rs` uses and stands off the larger (box stock at its circumscribed radius, cylinder at its radius). Hole mouths move out along their axis to the raw surface, bottoms unchanged (the drill feeds through the skin; Auto switches to full-retract pecking at r20). The stock's Z top sets the over-the-end-face route between opposite stations.\n- Every rapid is proved against stock radius + drill half-width (or above the stock top) and the job is refused by name if one fails; retracts back up a just-drilled hole are allowed.\n- Stock == part or no stock: falls back to the part, bit-identical output.\n- A cross drill's stamp includes the setup stock: resizing the stock after generating stales the op (before, the old hops would post).\n- `drilling_cross_spindle.rs` fixture now takes its stock from the bar (it tests the spindle frame alone; a world-centred box read as raw stock broke the #67 comparison).\n\n**After**: start, approach and station-change rapids all at r25 (stock r20 + 5 mm); the mill-turn program posts clear.\n\n**Pinned by** `drilling_cross_stock::{a_cross_drill_on_raw_stock_wider_than_the_part_hops_outside_the_stock, a_cross_drill_with_the_stock_equal_to_the_part_drills_the_part_only_chain, a_station_change_whose_chord_would_clip_the_bar_is_refused_by_name, re_sizing_the_raw_stock_stales_the_cross_drill_and_the_post_refuses_it}`.\n\n**Gates**: quick gate green vs the #67 branch (app 335 s, ui 333 s); the agent ran drilling_cross 9, drilling_cross_spindle 3, drilling_cross_stock 4, drilling_axial 7, lathe_spindle_law 8, lathe_post 5, lathe_post_refusals 5, posting 17, conformance 5, golden_cl 23, verify 21, operations 117, clippy -D warnings - green; drilling_cross and goldens not edited.\n\n**Follow-ups**: #79 (post-gate rapid check blind for radial programs), #80 (lathe cross drills falsely refused by the axial check), #81 (quarter-turn hop assumes on-centre holes).\n\nChangelog: fix(app): cross drill stands off the larger of the raw stock and the part, so no rapid between stations passes through uncut stock; refuses by name any rapid that would; resizing the stock stales the op\n\nFixes #77\n\n",
